[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: While the previous update synchronized unexecuted nodes to NodeState.PENDING in WaveScheduler._sync_states, several unreachable statements and defensive branches remain in the implementation: in DAG._find_cycle, the check for downstream nodes missing from _nodes is unreachable because all registered downstream nodes are maintained within _nodes; in DAG.add_edge and DAG.remove_node, the broad exception handlers around WaveScheduler singleton resolution and state synchronization represent caller assumptions guaranteed by the lifecycle environment; in DAG.validate, the secondary check for missing upstream nodes is redundant and unreachable after validating node definition dependencies; in DAG.topological_sort, the fallback cycle extraction branch when _find_cycle returns None is unreachable; in WaveScheduler._sync_states, the state deletion branch for nodes missing from the active graph is unreachable because remove_node directly purges scheduling state; in WaveScheduler.is_finished, the unexecuted blocked node completion fallback is unreachable under valid graph states; and in DAGRunner.run, the empty wave break condition is unreachable while is_finished evaluates to False. Please eliminate the unreachable code or annotate impossible branches with # pragma: no cover (assumption: <reason>).
[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: While the previous update restricted add_node dependency synchronization to unexecuted states and preserved running and terminal states, the pretense suite still lacks unit test coverage and state machine transitions for several public contract postconditions and error branches. Specifically, test coverage is missing for: DAG.add_edge raising NodeNotFoundError when an upstream node exists but the downstream node is absent; DAG.remove_node executed on a node with registered dependent downstream nodes to assert postconditions removing incident edges and updating dependent definitions; DAG.topological_sort raising NodeNotFoundError when graph definitions reference nonexistent dependencies; DAG.compute_critical_path on an empty graph returning an empty path and zero duration; WaveScheduler.mark_failed propagating SKIPPED status across multi-level transitive downstream dependents under SKIP_DOWNSTREAM and CONTINUE_ON_ERROR; WaveScheduler.is_finished returning True when the graph contains no nodes and returning False when any node is in RUNNING state; and WaveScheduler.get_state raising NodeNotFoundError when querying an absent node identifier.
